msgid "## Design Principles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"title: Sleep\n"
"---\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:6
msgid "# Sleep Mechanism"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:8
msgid ""
"> Light Sleep is the incremental extraction channel (semantic + limbic + "
"autobiographical); Deep Sleep optimizes semantic memory inventory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:10
msgid "## Overview"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:12
msgid ""
"Sleep is the digital life's memory consolidation mechanism—analogous to "
"human sleep where the brain replays daytime experiences, converts short-term "
"memory to long-term storage; the consolidation process itself dissipates, "
"leaving no trace."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:19
msgid ""
"**Internal mechanism, no trace** — Sleep runs in background, does not write "
"to sessions, does not affect conversation flow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:19
msgid ""
"**Do not copy human rhythm literally** — Triggered by system need (cron), "
"not real-time"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:19
msgid ""
"**Two-tier layering** — Light sleep (incremental writes), deep sleep "
"(semantic inventory optimization)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:19
msgid ""
"**Identity context** — All memory processing must carry **self layer six "
"blocks** + resident memory (see [`self-layer.md`](self-layer.md))"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:21
msgid "## Current State"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Mechanism              | Status         | Notes                                         |\n"
"| ---------------------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Sleep cycle pipeline   | ✅ Implemented | Single cron `builtin-sleep-cycle` @ 02:00     |\n"
"| Light sleep (in-cycle) | ✅ Implemented | Step `light-sleep` in sleep-cycle DAG         |\n"
"| Deep sleep (in-cycle)  | ✅ Implemented | Step `deep-sleep`, depends on light-sleep     |\n"
"| Memory ref sync        | ✅ Implemented | Step `memory-ref-sync`, depends on deep-sleep |\n"
"| Self-layer refresh     | ✅ Implemented | Step `self-layer-refresh`, after light-sleep  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:31
msgid "## Orchestration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:33
msgid ""
"Sleep uses a **macro DAG** (`sleep-cycle` pipeline) orchestrated by "
"`PipelineRunner` (`@freeanima/runtime/pipeline`). A single cron job triggers "
"the full cycle; step order and dependencies are explicit in code ([`platform/"
"src/boot/sleep-cycle.ts`](../../platform/src/boot/sleep-cycle.ts))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Light sleep** and **deep sleep** keep their **internal** multi-stage / multi-round sequencing inside `runLightSleep()` / `runDeepSleep()` — not promoted to macro DAG nodes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:37
msgid ""
"Chamber WebUI (`/webui/chamber/sleep`) supports **diagnostic** runs: full "
"cycle or individual steps (`force` skips dependency checks)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:39
msgid ""
"Pipeline run state is persisted at `~/.anima/runtime/pipeline_sleep-"
"cycle_run.json` (SSOT for step status; no EventBus)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:41
msgid "## Light Sleep"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Attribute     | Value                                                                           |\n"
"| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Trigger       | Sleep-cycle step `light-sleep` (cron @ 02:00 or Chamber diagnostics)            |\n"
"| Scope         | Sessions with activity in previous calendar day                                 |\n"
"| Input         | Full day's conversations (user+assistant, tools stripped), segmented by session |\n"
"| Orchestration | Three stages sequential (separate LLM calls each)                               |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:50
msgid "### Three Stages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Stage              | Target                       | Purpose                                                                                  |\n"
"| ------------------ | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| 1 Semantic         | Semantic memory              | Extract facts, preferences, experiences from dialogue                                    |\n"
"| 2 Limbic           | Emotional anchors            | Capture session mood and emotional turning points                                        |\n"
"| 3 Autobiographical | Autobiographical narrative   | Record what experiences meant to the digital life                                        |\n"
"| 3b                 | Autobiography summary (self) | Compress narratives into grouped self-layer outline (title-only bullets by significance) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Restraint principle:** Each stage LLM may judge \"nothing worth recording\" → no writes; program still runs subsequent stages.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Dedup (semantic):** Compare only against existing memories from same source sessions; cross-thread merging left to deep sleep.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:63
msgid "## Deep Sleep"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:69
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Attribute  | Value                                                                                                |\n"
"| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Trigger    | Sleep-cycle step `deep-sleep` (after light-sleep in DAG)                                             |\n"
"| Target     | All active semantic memory                                                                           |\n"
"| Operations | Contradiction detection + expiry marking, split, dedup merge, pin maintenance—four sequential rounds |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:71
msgid "### Four Rounds"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Round | Intent                                   |\n"
"| ----- | ---------------------------------------- |\n"
"| 1     | Contradiction detection + expiry marking |\n"
"| 2     | Split multi-fact entries                 |\n"
"| 3     | Dedup merge similar entries              |\n"
"| 4     | Pin maintenance (keep pinned ≤ 20)       |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ordering rationale:** Clean problems first, then refine, then merge, then trim resident pins.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:82
msgid "### Contradiction Definition (Exclusive)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:84
msgid ""
"Two memories semantically negate each other and cannot be explained by "
"temporal change → contradiction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:88
msgid ""
"✓ Contradiction: \"daughter born Year of Tiger\" vs \"daughter born Year of "
"Goat\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:88
msgid ""
"✗ Not contradiction: \"likes apples\" vs \"likes cherries\" (can coexist)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:88
msgid ""
"✗ Not contradiction (change): \"likes Python\" vs \"now prefers TypeScript\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:90
msgid "## Trigger Mechanism"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:94
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```cron\n"
"0 2 * * *  sleep-cycle   # builtin-sleep-cycle: light → deep → self-layer-refresh ∥ memory-ref-sync\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:96
msgid "DAG (macro layer):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"light-sleep\n"
"  ├─► deep-sleep ──► memory-ref-sync (optional step)\n"
"  └─► self-layer-refresh (optional step)\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:104
msgid "After downtime, the next scheduled run catches up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compression** stays session-scoped (turn-time `advanceCompressionMeta`); it is **not** a sleep-cycle step. Nightly consolidation does not replace per-session compression.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:108
msgid "## Historical Backfill (Chamber WebUI)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:110
msgid ""
"For historical conversations before go-live or after migration, use "
"**Chamber → Sleep records** (`/webui/chamber/sleep`):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:115
msgid "Open the **Historical light sleep backfill** card"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:115
msgid ""
"Optionally set **From** / **To** (CST calendar days, `YYYY-MM-DD`); defaults "
"match the 02:00 cron (earliest session → yesterday)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:115
msgid ""
"Check **Resume from saved progress** to continue from `~/.anima/runtime/"
"light_sleep_backfill_state.json`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:115
msgid "Click **Start backfill**; progress polls automatically while running"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Field      | Description                                                          |\n"
"| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **From**   | Start date; if omitted, earliest session day in archive              |\n"
"| **To**     | End date; if omitted, **yesterday** (same as 02:00 cron default day) |\n"
"| **Resume** | Continue from progress file, skip completed days                     |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:123
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Behavior notes:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:128
msgid ""
"Each day independently processed; single-day failure recorded then continue"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:128
msgid "Autobiography summary refresh runs on **last day** by default"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:128
msgid ""
"Backfill writes semantic / limbic / autobiographical; **cross-session merge "
"still relies on deep sleep**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:128
msgid ""
"No conflict with 02:00 cron, but pause service during early-morning backfill "
"if possible"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:130
msgid "## Relationship to Existing Architecture"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"Conversation archive\n"
"  │ sleep-cycle pipeline (02:00)\n"
"  │   step light-sleep (three internal stages)\n"
"  ├─► semantic memory\n"
"  ├─► emotional anchors\n"
"  └─► autobiographical narrative ──compress──► self-layer autobiography summary (grouped outline)\n"
"  │\n"
"  │   step deep-sleep (four internal rounds)\n"
"  ▼\n"
"semantic memory (consolidated)\n"
"  │   step memory-ref-sync\n"
"  │ memory_recall (real-time retrieval in conversation)\n"
"  ▼\n"
"Agent identity and recalled fragments in current context\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:149
msgid "## `memory_remember` Tool"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:150
msgid ""
"In-conversation `memory_remember` is a convenience wrapper for creating "
"semantic memory during dialogue. Soft deprecation via deprecate action; "
"physical delete also supported."
msgstr ""
